content.text:
Here’s a ready‑to‑paste CSS snippet you can add to **admin.css** (or a separate stylesheet that’s loaded after it) to make the analytics cards sit tighter side‑by‑side and stay horizontal on a broader range of viewports:

```css
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Make .analytics‑grid tighter and keep two columns on larger screens
   ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

/* 1️⃣ Reduce the space between the two cards */
.analytics-grid {
  gap: var(--space-3) !important;   /* 12 px instead of 16 px */
}

/* 2️⃣ Keep the two‑column layout down to a narrower breakpoint
      (so the cards don’t stack as early) */
@media (max-width: 1100px) {        /* adjust as you prefer */
  .analytics-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr !important;
  }
}

/* 3️⃣ Optional: shrink the internal padding for a more compact card */
.analytics-card-header,
.analytics-card-body {
  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4) !important;  /* was var(--space-4)/var(--space-5) */
}

/* 4️⃣ Optional: reduce the chart height to keep the cards shorter */
.analytics-chart-wrapper {
  height: 180px !important;  /* was 220px */
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------
   If you want *all* UI elements (including analytics cards) to adopt
   the built‑in “compact mode”, just add the attribute to <html>:

   <html data‑compact="true">…</html>

   The stylesheet already defines tighter spacing, font sizes, and radii
   under [data‑compact="true"], so you won’t need any extra CSS.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
```

### How to use it
1. **Paste the block** at the bottom of `C:\Users\ADMIN\Desktop\TEST\assets\css\admin.css` (or in a new file you import after it).  
2. **Save the file** – the changes take effect immediately when the page reloads.  
3. **Fine‑tune** the numbers (`1100px` breakpoint, `180px` chart height, etc.) to suit your visual preference.

These tweaks keep the original markup untouched while delivering a tighter, side‑by‑side analytics layout that remains readable on most desktop widths. Feel free to adjust any of the values to get the exact density you want.
